@startuml
' Yang Shuo with OpenAI Codex assistance. #641; DG 5.1.
' Trace: CanonicalPeopleSession.execute; RoleAwareAddParser.parse; FieldValueTokenizer.
!include feature-sequence-style.iuml
participant "session :\nCanonicalPeopleSession" as S
participant "parser :\nRoleAwareAddParser" as P
participant "<<class>>\nFieldValueTokenizer" as T

S -> S : Consume and clear\npending deletion
S -> S : Extract word; look up\ncommand definition
alt protected and route unavailable
  note over S : Reject before argument parsing.
else allowed route, valid single-line input
  S -> P : parse(arguments)\n[add example]
  P -> T : tokenize role-aware fields
  note over T
    Lowercase prefixes; preserve name s/o, d/o
    and digit-surrounded address slashes.
  end note
  T --> P : prefix boundaries
  P -> P : Validate prefixes, required\nfields and domain values
  alt invalid fields or values
    P --> S : ParseException with guidance
  else valid input
    P --> S : PersonAdditionInput\n(no allocated ID)
    ref over S : Execute the parsed command\n(5.2 and Figure 5.2a)
  end
end
note over S, T
  Empty, unknown and multiline input are rejected.
  The enum switch selects the other typed parsers;
  read queries route directly to their handlers.
end note
@enduml
